  "facts": [
    "Construction of the Lincoln Tunnel stretched from 1934 to 1957, with the central tube debuting in 1937, the northern tube opening in 1945, and the southern tube following in 1957 after wartime delays.",
    "The center tube of the Lincoln Tunnel houses two reversible lanes that can shift direction for peak traffic, while trucks are barred and all vehicles must fit within an 8‑foot‑6‑inch width limit.",
    "Weehawken’s Route 495 Helix, a 4,000‑foot, three‑quarters‑circle viaduct, climbs the steep King's Bluff to the tunnel portal, earning a reputation as one of the East Coast’s most congested corridors with 3.4 million hours lost annually."
  ],
